      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Adjunct Instructor, Civil Engineering | . page has loaded. Adjunct Instructor, Civil Engineering | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Adjunct Instructor, Civil Engineering Print Apply ﻿ Adjunct Instructor, Civil Engineering Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Part-Time Adjunct Job Number 202600360 Home Org Civil Engineering Opening Date 07/06/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Job Summary The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at Lamar University invites applications for Adjunct Faculty positions to teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Civil and Environmental Engineering. Adjunct faculty are appointed on a semester-by-semester basis based on departmental instructional needs. Successful candidates will provide high-quality instruction and support student success while working collaboratively with the department faculty. Essential Job Functions Prepare and deliver assigned undergraduate and/or graduate Civil and Environmental Engineering courses. Develop instructional materials, evaluate student learning, maintain course records, and submit grades according to university deadlines. Maintain communication with students and the department regarding course-related matters. Attend required meetings and complete administrative responsibilities associated with assigned courses. Other duties may be assigned to this position on a regular or occasional basis to respond to the needs of the university. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate engineering courses. Strong oral and written communication skills. Ability to effectively engage and mentor students. Commitment to fostering a supportive, respectful, and student-centered learning environment that promotes student success. Desired Qualifications: Previous college-level teaching experience. Professional engineering industry experience. Professional Engineer (PE) license preferred. Experience using learning management systems and instructional technology. Expertise in one or more areas of Civil and Environmental Engineering, including but not limited to structural, geotechnical, environmental, transportation, water resources, construction, or surveying. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Teach assigned undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Civil and Environmental Engineering. Prepare course materials, syllabi, assignments, and examinations. Evaluate student performance and submit grades in accordance with university deadlines. Maintain regular communication with students and respond to inquiries in a timely manner. Strong oral and written communication skills. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 25 lbs and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks, including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing, and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: Work is performed in a classroom, laboratory, office, and/or online instructional settings. Teaching assignments may include day, evening, weekend, or online courses. Adjunct appointments are temporary and contingent upon departmental needs, student enrollment, and available funding. Regular interaction with students, faculty, and staff is required. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. This position is not eligible for benefits. Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assista