      "title": "Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment | . page has loaded. Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment Print Apply ﻿ Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment Salary $52,446.00 - $68,180.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600253 Home Org Inst Energy & Petro Ind Eng Stu Svc Opening Date 07/16/2026 Closing Date Continuous FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment holds a pivotal role within the College of Engineering and the Engineering Institute for Energy and Petrochemical Industries (EPI) at Lamar University. Reporting directly to the Director of Operations, this position is instrumental in advancing the recruitment and branding efforts of the College. The Associate Director is responsible for developing, maintaining, and evaluating the annual recruitment plan, with a particular focus on attracting top-tier undergraduate students to the COE and EPI. This role also involves nurturing and managing essential partnerships with community-based organizations, high schools, technical centers, 2-year colleges, and businesses to expand the reach of engineering programs. The Associate Director actively engages with various community stakeholders to create activities and programs designed to prepare students for successful college enrollment. The position also plays a vital role in managing the organization of various off and on campus recruitment visits and events. In addition to these external outreach efforts, the Associate Director offers essential student support by professionally corresponding with prospective students, providing guidance on pre-college preparation requirements, and assisting with the application process. Collaboration with the Lamar University Marketing Team is essential to execute impactful marketing campaigns that elevate the visibility and appeal of the COE and EPI. Collaboration with the Lamar University Enrollment Services Team is essential to execute impactful recruitment that elevate the visibility and appeal of the COE and EPI. The Associate Director is responsible for designing, ordering, and distributing marketing materials, maintaining an inventory of branded items for special events, and creating newsletters to keep students and stakeholders informed about engineering developments. The role also includes the management and maintenance of COE webpages, maximizing the use of social media for student and industry spotlights, and fostering a consistent brand image across all materials. Overall, this position plays a critical role in driving recruitment, marketing, and branding initiatives to support the success and growth of the College of Engineering at Lamar University. The Associate Director of Marketing and Recruitment is a dynamic and influential position that shapes the future of engineering education at Lamar University, attracting and retaining top talent in engineering programs and promoting a strong brand presence for the COE and EPI. Essential Job Functions Lead and guide the marketing, recruitment, visits, and events teams, overseeing their respective functions and ensuring cohesive collaboration. Develop, maintain, and evaluate comprehensive annual plans for recruitment, visits, and events to attract top-tier students and industry partners to the College of Engineering (COE) and the Engineering Institute for Energy and Petrochemical Industries (EPI). Cultivate and manage partnerships with community-based organizations, high schools, technical centers, 2-year colleges, and industry to expand the reach and visibility of COE and EPI through on-campus and off-campus activities. Gather, analyze, and leverage data to evaluate the effectiveness of recruitment, visit, and event strategies, providing data-driven recommendations for enhancements to meet enrollment and partnership goals. Manage budgets for the marketing, recruitment, visits, and events departments, ensuring responsible financial planning and allocation of resources to support departmental goals. Collaborate closely with Office of Operations leadership to ensure alignment of departmental activities with institutional objectives, contributing to the overall success of the College of Engineering and Lamar University. Oversee staff organizing and promote both on-campus and off-campus recruitment visits, events, and experiences to attract prospective students and industry partners, collaborating with admissions for undergraduate student recruitment. Assume responsibility for branding efforts, maintaining a consistent brand image across all marketing materials, communications, and on-campus experiences. Oversee that the team is corresponding professionally with prospective students and industry partners, offering guidance and support throughout the application, enrollment, and partnership processes. Oversee the creation and dissemination of internal and external communications, including newsletters and marketing publications, to inform stakeholders about engineering developments, initiatives, and achievements. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree in Marketing, Engineering, Higher Education, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field is essential. 3 or more years of progressive higher education experience or related marketing/recruiting field. 3 or more years of supervisory and leadership skills. Official transcripts are required at the time of employment. Desired Qualifications: A master’s degree in Marketing, Engineering, Education, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field. Prior experience in a college recruitment and event environment, demonstrating a familiarity with the details and demands of marketing, student outreach, enrollment, yield, and retention. Demonstrated success in developing and executing strategic marketing plans to meet recruitment goals and enhance an institution's brand presence. Strong data analysis skills with the ability to monitor and report on key performance indicators, utilizing data-driven insights to improve strategies. Previous involvement in college marketing showcases the ability to plan, coordinate, and execute various recruitment initiatives related to academic institutions. Skill in designing and distributing marketing publications, ensuring high-quality materials in alignment with institutional standards. Proficiency and experience in utilizing a range of technologies, which may encompass, but are not limited to, systems like Banner, MyScholarships, various social media platforms, event design platforms, purchasing systems, event reservation platforms, Customer Relationship Management (CRM) systems/Slate, etc. Proficiency in advanced technical and computer skills to support administrative functions, including but not limited to the MS Office Suite, with a strong focus on PowerPoint, Excel, and database management. Familiarity with electronic calendar management and various videoconferencing applications like Outlook, Zoom, MS Teams, MS Office, Slate, etc. Proficiency in digital marketing, social media management, publication design, and content creation to effectively promote academic programs and institutions. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Demonstrates strong supervisory, management, and relationship-building skills. Must be able to effectively direct existing, comprehensive enrollment and retention programs, and to develop new ones on his/her own initiative. Dependability, creativity, good judgment, professionalism, and dedication to sound principles of student development are paramount among the necessary characteristics for this position. Detail-oriented. Timely completion of duties. Proficient in delivering the highest quality of customer service when engaging with industry leaders, representatives, faculty, staff, and students. Possesses excellent written and verbal communication skills, including strong editing and proofreading capabilities, and is adept at interacting with staff at all organizational levels. Strategic planning/visioning aptitude. Understanding and appreciation of engineering. Budget management/fundraising background. Knowledge of growing role technology plays in the delivery of recruitment, marketing, and event management. Physical Requirements: Lifting and Carrying: The ability to lift and move reams/boxes of paper, tables, decorations, and other supplies, weighing up to 50lbs, as necessary for job tasks. Event Setup and Teardown: Must be capable of setting up and tearing down equipment and materials for events, which may involve bending, lifting, and carrying. Extended Periods on Feet: This position may require long hours spent standing during events. Candidates should be able to stand, walk, and perform job duties for extended periods. Walking Campus: Ability to walk around the campus, including participating in visits and camps, which may involve traversing various terrains and buildings. Job Conditions: 8 am – 5 pm Monday-Friday, some early mornings, some evenings, some weekends. This is an on-campus position. This position requires participation and possibly attendance at all College of Engineering and Engineering Institute for Energy and Petrochemical Industries (EPI) events. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance? Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents. Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays.? To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you hold a Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Engineering, Higher Education, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field? Yes No 02 Do you have three (3) or more years of progressive experience in higher education or a related marketing or recruitment field? Yes No 03 Do you have three (3) or more years of supervisory and leadership experience? Yes No 04 Are you able to provide official transcripts at the time of employment if selected? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with the