      "title": "Associate Director, Student Recruitment",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Associate Director, Student Recruitment | . page has loaded. Associate Director, Student Recruitment | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Associate Director, Student Recruitment Print Apply ﻿ Associate Director, Student Recruitment Salary $58,739.00 - $76,361.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600286 Home Org Area Recruiting Opening Date 08/24/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Associate Director of Admissions, Recruitment provides strategic leadership for the university’s recruitment efforts across freshman, graduate, and international student populations. This position is responsible for developing, implementing, and assessing comprehensive recruitment and yield strategies to meet institutional enrollment goals. The Associate Director supervises and develops Assistant Directors, ensuring effective execution of recruitment initiatives and alignment with university priorities. Essential Job Functions Develop, implement, and continuously refine a comprehensive recruitment strategy and annual plan that aligns with institutional enrollment goals across freshman, graduate, and international student populations; ensure effective execution through Assistant Directors and recruitment staff. Provide direct supervision, coaching, and performance management for Assistant Directors by establishing clear expectations, monitoring progress toward goals, and fostering a high-performing and collaborative team environment . Utilize Slate to monitor funnel performance, assess the effectiveness of recruitment initiatives, and adjust strategies to meet enrollment targets. Recommend and implement improvements to recruitment communications, marketing strategies, and student engagement efforts to effectively articulate the university’s value proposition and attract prospective students aligned with enrollment goals. Partner with academic colleges, graduate programs, international programs, marketing, and student services to align recruitment messaging, improve yield strategies, and enhance the prospective student experience from inquiry through enrollment. Provide strategic oversight and direction for recruitment events, travel, special programs, and key initiatives; ensure alignment with enrollment priorities, efficient resource utilization, and consistent execution across student populations. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree. 4 years of progressive recruitment, admissions, and/or higher education experience required. Other relevant leadership experience may substitute. Desired Qualifications: Master’s degree in Leadership, Business Management, Higher Education, or similar preferred. Prior management and leadership experience preferred. Experience and knowledge of Slate or other CRM systems preferred. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Leadership & Team Development: Ability to lead, coach, and develop professional staff, including managing through others and fostering accountability, collaboration, and high performance. Data-Informed Strategy: Ability to analyze data to inform strategy, monitor performance, and adjust tactics to meet enrollment goals. Strategic Communication & Messaging: Ability to communicate effectively across various audiences through clear, persuasive written, verbal, and presentation skills. Judgement & Decision-Making: Ability to exercise discretion and sound judgement in handling sensitive student information, personnel matters, and organizational priorities. Collaboration & Cross-Functional Engagement: Ability to build strong working relationships across divisions (academic colleges, graduate programs, international offices, marketing, etc.) to support recruitment goals. Adaptability & Innovation: Demonstrated flexibility and a proactive mindset in responding to changing enrollment trends, technologies, and student needs. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift, load, and transport recruitment materials, displays, and other equipment up to 35 pounds. Job Conditions: Ability to travel and work a varied schedule with flexible hours, including some weekends and evenings. Enrollment in and successful completion of MGMT 3311 Leadership Essentials within the first six months of employment. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance. Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents. Paid time off, vacation, sick, and holidays. To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No 02 Do you have at least 4 years of progressive experience in recruitment, admissions, and/or higher education? Yes No 03 If not, do you have other relevant leadership experience that could substitute for this requirement? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not