      "title": "Certified HVAC/R Technician",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Certified HVAC/R Technician | . page has loaded. Certified HVAC/R Technician | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Certified HVAC/R Technician Print Apply ﻿ Certified HVAC/R Technician Salary $41,809.00 - $54,352.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600411 Home Org Building Maintenance Opening Date 08/20/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary Under the direction of the HVAC Supervisor, the HVAC Technician is responsible for the installation, inspection, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of commercial and industrial HVAC systems and related equipment. This position works with a variety of equipment, including air handlers, fan coil units, VAV boxes, recirculation pumps, package units, gas-fired boilers, ice machines, chillers, compressors, and central plant systems. The incumbent applies knowledge of HVAC, electrical, and plumbing systems to diagnose and resolve equipment issues while ensuring the reliable operation of campus facilities. The position requires proficiency in the use of Microsoft Office applications, email, and computerized maintenance management systems (CMMS) to document work activities and support maintenance operations. The HVAC Technician collaborates with other trades, monitors contracted work, provides guidance and training to subordinate employees, and delivers exceptional customer service to faculty, staff, students, and visitors. As a representative of Facilities Management and the University, the incumbent is expected to maintain the highest standards of professionalism, ethics, teamwork, and appearance. This position is designated as essential personnel and may be required to work during emergency situations or University closures. Essential Job Functions HVAC Maintenance and Repairs Perform troubleshooting, diagnostics, preventive maintenance, and repairs on commercial and industrial HVAC systems, central plant equipment, and related mechanical, electrical, and plumbing components. Work Order Management and Documentation Review, prioritize, and complete assigned work orders; document maintenance activities, labor, materials, and equipment information using the CMMS and other required systems. Preventive Maintenance and Equipment Reliability Implement and support preventive maintenance programs to maximize equipment performance, reliability, efficiency, and service life. Customer Service, Collaboration, and Training Collaborate with other trades, contractors, faculty, staff, and students to resolve maintenance issues; provide excellent customer service and assist with training and mentoring team members as assigned. Safety, Compliance, and Emergency Response Maintain compliance with safety regulations, complete required training, monitor contractor work as assigned, and participate in emergency response activities and essential operations during university closures or emergencies. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or equivalent. Associate degree in HVAC or a related field or completion of a formal technical training program with certification n HVAC. A minimum of three (3) years of progressively responsible experience in heating, ventilation, air conditioning, or a closely related field. Desired Qualifications: Commercial HVAC experience particularly in central plan operations. Working knowledge of gas-fired boilers, chillers, cooling towers, and related mechanical systems is preferred. Experience using a computerized maintenance management system for maintenance planning, work order management an asset tracking is preferred. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Knowledge of HVAC systems, equipment, maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair procedures. Working knowledge of electrical and plumbing systems as they relate to HVAC diagnostics and repairs. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and email systems. Ability to diagnose problems, evaluate solutions, and perform repairs effectively. Strong customer service skills with the ability to interact professionally with faculty, staff, students, and stakeholders. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team to support departmental and university goals. Demonstrated commitment to high ethical standards, professionalism, and accountability. Physical Requirements: Tasks require the regular and, at times, sustained performance of moderately physically demanding work. Some combination of climbing and balancing, to include climbing ladders, stooping, kneeling, crawling, working at heights and working in confined spaces. May involve the lifting of moderately heavy objects, up to 45 pounds. Requires a full range of physical motion to operate manual/electrically powered tools. Job Conditions: Performance of essential functions may require exposure to adverse environmental conditions, such as dirt, dust, pollen, odors, wetness, humidity, weather, fumes, temperature and noise extremes, hazardous materials, machinery, vibrations, traffic hazards, or toxic agents. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a high school diploma or equivalent? Yes No 02 Do you have an Associate degree in HVAC OR a related field OR completion of a formal technical training program with certification in HVAC? Yes No 03 Do you have a minimum of 3 years of progressively responsible experience in heating, ventilation, air conditioning, or a closely related field? Yes No 04 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy 