      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Post Doctoral Researcher | . page has loaded. Post Doctoral Researcher | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Post Doctoral Researcher Print Apply ﻿ Post Doctoral Researcher Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number 202600471 Home Org Inst Energy & Petro Ind Eng Researc Opening Date 09/09/2026 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Postdoctoral Research Associate will support applied research conducted through the Center for Midstream Management and Science . The position will contribute to multiple projects involving midstream energy systems, pipelines, leak detection, emissions, instrumentation, laboratory measurements, and data analysis. The research will be conducted in the lab and in the field. The postdoctoral researcher will help design and conduct experiments, operate research equipment, analyze data, prepare technical deliverables, and support the development of new research methods. Assignments may change as CMMS develops new projects and industry partnerships. The position is therefore intended for a researcher who can work across several technical areas and quickly learn new systems. This is a temporary position with an initial appointment of one year. The position may be renewed for one additional year, contingent upon satisfactory performance and continued approval, for a maximum appointment of two years. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Applied Research and Project Execution: Conduct applied research in support of CMMS-sponsored and faculty-led projects. Design experiments, develop research methods, and evaluate new technologies. Manage assigned activities according to project schedules, objectives, and sponsor requirements. Laboratory and Field Measurements: Operate, calibrate, and troubleshoot laboratory and field measurement equipment. Conduct measurements involving leak detection, gases, emissions, sensors, and other project variables. Maintain experimental records and follow established safety and quality procedures. Data Analysis and Technical Development: Process, analyze, and interpret experimental and operational data. Develop scripts, models, software, or visualization tools needed for research projects. Evaluate data quality, measurement uncertainty, and system performance. Research Collaboration and Project Support: Work with CMMS faculty, staff, students, and industry partners on multidisciplinary projects. Contribute to technical reports, publications, proposals, presentations, and sponsor deliverables. Provide technical guidance to students and assist with laboratory and project activities. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Terminal degree in engineering, physics, chemistry, or a closely related STEM discipline at the level of PhD or DE. Experience conducting experimental or applied research in an academic, laboratory, field, or industrial setting. Ability to plan experiments, collect and analyze data, and document research methods and results. Experience preparing technical reports, presentations, or peer-reviewed publications. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to multidisciplinary research teams. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Strong background in mathematics up to partial differential equations in three dimensions in solving the Helmholtz Equation in different coordinate systems, including cylindrical symmetries and applications of Bessel functions. Ability to manage multiple research tasks and meet project schedules and sponsor requirements. Willingness to travel for conducting research in the field across the Nation. Ability to present results at workshops, symposia, and conferences. Desired Qualifications: Experience with laboratory measurement systems such as mass spectrometry, gas chromatography, gas analyzers, or vacuum equipment. Experience with sensors, instrumentation, data-acquisition systems, or automated experimental equipment. Experience with programming, signal processing, statistical analysis, machine learning, or scientific data visualization. Experience conducting field tests or working with industry-sponsored research projects. Familiarity with laboratory safety, calibration procedures, quality control, and experimental uncertainty. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Ability to design, conduct, and troubleshoot laboratory and field experiments. Ability to learn and operate unfamiliar instruments, software, and research systems. Strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret complex experimental data. Ability to document procedures, code, equipment configurations, and research findings clearly. Ability to collaborate with faculty, students, technical staff, industry partners, and project sponsors. Ability to oversee research projects for undergraduate and graduate students. Strong organizational skills and attention to experimental quality and safety. Ability to publish results across the spectrum of trade journals to high-impact journals. Physical Requirements: Able to lift 25 pounds and be able to perform a variety of physical tasks including lifting, bending, stooping, squatting, stair climbing, and walking between buildings. Job Conditions: Work is typically performed in a lab or office environment. Occasional visits to field testing sites will be required. Flexibility in working hours may be needed during experimental deployments or system upgrades. Required Documents: Please note you MUST have these documents attached to your application to be considered complete. Cover Letter with a link to your PhD thesis Resume/Curriculum Vitae Transcripts from PhD program Research Statement 3 Letters of Reference, one of which must come from your PhD advisor Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students , Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120 -degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders,demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance . Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have a Terminal degree in engineering, physics, chemistry, or a closely related STEM discipline at the level of PhD or DE? Yes No 02 Do you have experience conducting experimental or applied research in an academic, laboratory, field, or industrial setting? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. . Careers at Lamar University Menu Close Menu . Careers at Lamar University Student & Hourly Job Openings Email Job Alerts Benefit Page New Hire Information Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy.