    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/lamar/jobs/5483397/gift-processing-specialist": {
      "title": "Gift Processing Specialist",
      "description": "Careers at Lamar University | . For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Gift Processing Specialist | . page has loaded. Gift Processing Specialist | . page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Careers at Lamar University Menu Careers at Lamar University Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. . powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Gift Processing Specialist Print Apply ﻿ Gift Processing Specialist Salary $37,330.00 - $48,529.00 Annually Location Beaumont, TX Job Type Full-Time Staff Job Number 202600450 Home Org University Advancement Opening Date 09/15/2026 FLSA Non-Exempt Description Benefits Questions Job Summary The Gift Processing Specialist serves as the primary administrator for the receipt, processing, recording, and acknowledgment of charitable contributions to Lamar University. This position ensures the accurate and timely recording of gifts and pledges; maintains compliance with university policies, CASE standards, IRS regulations, Texas State University System requirements, and State of Texas guidelines; and supports fundraising, donor stewardship, and reporting activities. The position serves as a key liaison among donors, University Advancement, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, and campus departments to ensure the integrity of gift records and donor data. Special Note: We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be authorized to work in the United States without the need for sponsorship now or in the future. Essential Job Functions Receive, review, process, and record all charitable contributions, including cash, checks, credit cards, ACH transactions, payroll deductions, matching gifts, pledges, and gifts-in-kind. Prepare deposit documentation, process gifts in the University Advancement database, generate donor acknowledgments and tax receipts, and ensure compliance with university gift acceptance policies, CASE standards, IRS regulations, TSUS requirements, and State of Texas guidelines. Analyze gifts and pledge documentation to determine appropriate campaign, appeal, fund, designation, and account coding; research and resolve gift-related discrepancies to ensure accurate recording and reporting. Generate and distribute gift, donor, pledge, and fundraising reports, including daily major gift reports, quarterly TSUS Board of Regents reports, and other reports supporting donor stewardship, fundraising, and compliance activities. Monitor and administer outstanding pledges and the corporate matching gift program by tracking commitments, processing matching requests, issuing reminders, conducting follow-up communications, and maintaining accurate records of pending and completed gifts. Collaborate with University Advancement staff, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, and other campus departments to ensure proper gift administration, payroll deduction processing, regulatory compliance, donor stewardship, and record management. Provide administrative and database support, including updating constituent records, processing correspondence and mail, responding to inquiries, maintaining online giving information, assisting with gift entry operations, and recommending process improvements to enhance efficiency and data integrity. Minimum and Desired Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Associate’s degree or two-year college equivalent or experience required or one to two (1-2) years of directly related experience. A minimum of two (2) years of experience in gift processing, donor services, advancement services, fundraising operations, accounting, or related administrative functions. Desired Qualifications: Experience in higher education, healthcare, foundation, or nonprofit fundraising environments. Knowledge of IRA charitable giving regulations and gift acceptance practices. Experience with electronic payment platforms and online giving systems. Supplemental Information Key Competencies: Strong attention to detail, accuracy, and dependability. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while meeting strict deadlines. Use of judgment, sensitivity, and discretion in handling confidential materials and situations. Excellent numerical, organization, proofreading, customer service, and written and oral communication skills required. Possess general office skills, business communication skills, and experience working with the public. Experience using computers including word processing and spreadsheets. Physical Requirements: The essential functions of this position require the capacity to remain seated for prolonged durations. Job Conditions: Standard work hours are Monday through Friday, 8:00 am – 5:00 pm. Occasional overtime may be required based on gift volume and the operational needs of the department. Who We Are: Home to more than 18,000 students, Lamar University is among the fastest growing Texas colleges and universities. LU is a member of The Texas State University System, which is the first higher education system of Texas and maintains the lowest average tuition and fees of any university system in Texas. With more than 120-degree options and a community that cares, Lamar students are always proud to be Cardinals. Lamar University strives to educate leaders, demonstrate excellence in student learning and career readiness, and pursue research with relevance. Lamar University is committed to fostering an environment of teamwork where all students, faculty, and staff can learn, work, and become a part of our community. Benefits: Health, dental & vision insurance Life insurance State of Texas Retirement plans Tuition covered at 100% for employees, spouses and/or eligible dependents Paid time off – vacation, sick, and holidays To see more information about the available benefits, please visit: Benefits - Lamar University Lamar University is An Equal Opportunity Employer Lamar University is proud to provide employment preference to veteran applicants in accordance with Texas 805 Government Code, Section 657.003. This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. 01 Do you have an Associate’s degree or two-year college equivalent or experience required or one to two (1-2) years of directly related experience? Yes No 02 Do you have a minimum of two (2) years of experience in gift processing, donor services, advancement services, fundraising operations, accounting, or related administrative functions? Yes No 03 Will you now or in the future require sponsorship? Yes No Required Question Employer Lamar University Address 1060 East Virginia St. Beaumont, Texas, 77705 Phone 409-880-8375 Website https://www.lamar.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Careers at Lamar University Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. . Careers at Lamar University Menu Close Menu . Careers at Lamar University Student & Hourly Job Openings Email Job Alerts Benefit Page New Hire Information Help & Support Translate SOCIAL Facebook LinkedIn Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data we collect or use, and applications owned or controlled by Governmentjobs.com, Inc. (DBA “NEOGOV”), including our related brands NEOGOV.com, NEOED.com, PowerDMS.com, Governmentjobs.com, Schooljobs.com, and our mobile app(s) (collectively referred to as the “Services”), or affiliated companies (collectively referred to herein as “Governmentjobs”, \"Schooljobs\", “NEOGOV”, “NEOED”, “PowerDMS”, “we”, “us”, or “our”). By using any part of the Services you agree that you have read this Policy, your personal data will be processed as described herein, and you agree to be bound by this Poli